# Construction editor overflow scrolling

Ensure ordered construction plans remain fully editable when their rows exceed the available screen height.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] The construction editor scrolls vertically when ordered rows extend below the viewport.
- [ ] Every construction row can be reached without being obscured permanently by the bottom action bar.
- [ ] The final-step bin, Clear, preview, and New Step controls remain reachable and interactive.
- [ ] The top player selector and preview placement remain consistent with SCR-004 while content scrolls beneath or below them as designed.
- [ ] Cancel and Save remain fixed, visible, and interactive throughout scrolling.
- [ ] Adding a step does not strand the new final row outside reachable scroll bounds.
- [ ] Cards-plan scrolling and layout remain unchanged.
- [ ] UI regression coverage compiles with enough mock steps to overflow a compact iPhone viewport.
- [ ] Focused UI checks pass on a functioning simulator.

## Scope notes

- The editor already contains a ScrollView; this task owns layout, insets, and regression behavior required for real overflow rather than replacing the navigation model.
